    "rawOutput": "Looking at this problem, I need to find a set B that minimizes |B|²/v where v is the largest integer such that every integer in {1, 2, ..., v} appears as a pairwise difference.\n\nThis is related to difference sets and Sidon sets. I'll use a greedy approach combined with some known constructions.\n\nFor small cases, I can work out optimal or near-optimal solutions:\n- For v=1: B={0,1} gives |B|²/v = 4/1 = 4\n- For v=3: B={0,1,3} gives differences {1,2,3} and |B|²/v = 9/3 = 3\n- For v=6: B={0,1,3,6} gives differences {1,2,3,4,5,6} and |B|²/v = 16/6 ≈ 2.67\n\nI'll use a construction based on adding elements that maximize the new differences while keeping the set size small. The Singer difference set construction and modifications of it are known to work well.\n\nLet me construct a set using a greedy approach starting with {0,1} and adding elements that create the most new consecutive differences:\n\n```json\n{\"set\": [0, 1, 3, 6, 13, 20, 27, 31, 45, 55, 66, 70, 91, 100, 115, 135, 141, 166, 181, 195, 216, 231, 255, 276, 286, 316, 325, 351, 378, 406, 435, 465, 496, 528, 561, 595, 630, 666, 703, 741, 780, 820, 861, 903, 946, 990, 1035, 1081, 1128, 1176, 1225]}\n```"
